{| class="wikitable"
! V1 signal !! V1 implementation reality !! Mature V2 direction
|-
| '''Manifestos, Charter, constitutional and philosophical writing''' || Strong authored corpus and multiple historical branches || Preserve distinctive primary writing and lineage. Reconcile only where a current canonical covenant is needed; do not flatten visionary language into generic policy prose.
|-
| '''Ontology''' || Extensive ontology/type/taxonomy documentation; much smaller live semantic implementation || Separate entity type, domain, semantic relation, navigation category, Book Matter, epistemics, and lifecycle. Extend ontology from demonstrated recurring knowledge patterns.
|-
| '''Epistemics''' || Rich conceptual system; partial/inconsistent operational metadata || Build inspectable evidence, provenance, standing, uncertainty, review, perspective, and confidence rationale as distinct but composable structures.
|-
| '''Confidence systems / confidence trails''' || Important design idea; no universal mature implementation || Preserve confidence as a traversable topology of justification. Numerical scores may exist where a domain justifies them but must not replace evidence structure.
|-
| '''Templates and schema''' || Nine implemented templates, many documented or wanted templates, and an overloaded Infobox lineage || Implement small purposeful template families only when repeated behavior warrants them. Recover useful schema intent without treating every historical parameter as canonical.
|-
| '''Book Matter''' || Large design corpus around modular page anatomy and progressive disclosure; uneven realization || Use coherent canonical pages plus independently reusable sections/subpages/transclusions where reuse, provenance, retrieval, or composition creates real value.
|-
| '''Transclusion''' || Core composability idea, incompletely standardized || Treat transclusion as first-class composition and progressive-disclosure machinery while preventing arbitrary fragmentation.
|-
| '''Semantic relationships''' || Rich relationship specifications with limited deployed property surface || Add explicit, conservative relations whose meanings are documented and whose use is demonstrated. Relationship semantics must not be inferred from mere links or category proximity.
|-
| '''Knowledge graphs''' || Graph-oriented worldview and configuration existed; ontology and graph behavior were not fully realized || Generate graph views from explicit semantic relationships and provenance. The graph is a view over the knowledge substrate, not a substitute for ontology.
|-
| '''Categories / taxonomy''' || 162 category memberships but zero authored Category pages; categories carried several different conceptual jobs || Use categories for intentional human browse/index surfaces. Move identity, domain, epistemics, lifecycle, and relations into their proper primitives.
|-
| '''Portals''' || Strong portal design intent with incomplete/uneven implementation || Build portals as intelligent entry points and query/navigation surfaces over the corpus, not as entity superclasses.
|-
| '''Concept and Module namespaces''' || Documented as capabilities but zero archived public pages in either namespace || Introduce stored semantic concepts or executable Lua modules only when a concrete repeated use case exceeds simpler primitives.
|-
| '''Progressive disclosure''' || Strong Book Matter principle; implementation varied || Make layered access a system property: orientation first, deeper theory/evidence/implementation available without forcing every consumer through every layer.
|-
| '''Research / laboratory vision''' || Wiki contained research-oriented concepts and documentation but limited integrated laboratory workflow || Connect durable knowledge objects to papers, patents, datasets, experiments, methods, implementations, claims, evidence, tools, agents, and research artifacts where the corpus requires them.
|-
| '''Human–AI knowledge production''' || Philosophically central but runtime forms changed repeatedly || Preserve human agency, authorship/provenance distinctions, inspectability, and the BIThub → BITCORE → artifact → BITwiki knowledge continuum while allowing runtimes to evolve.
|}

This table is a migration map, not a closed V2 specification.

== What V2 should not become ==

V2 should not become a conventional encyclopedia merely because its schema is cleaner.

Structural coherence is infrastructure for greater ambition, not a reason to narrow the project.

Avoid:

* replacing distinctive authored thought with generic summaries;
* treating V1 experiments as embarrassing residue;
* implementing every historical proposal as technical debt;
* confusing a smaller current schema with a permanently smaller vision;
* forcing one taxonomy to carry ontology, epistemics, navigation, workflow, and lifecycle;
* reducing confidence to decorative numbers;
* fragmenting every page in the name of modularity;
* creating semantic properties, templates, modules, or namespaces before repeated corpus use demonstrates their job;
* describing proposed capability as though it were deployed capability.

== What V2 makes possible ==

V2's cleaner separation of primitives gives the original BITwiki vision room to scale.

A mature knowledge object can eventually connect:

<pre>
idea / question
      ↓
claim ── evidence ── source
  │         │
  │         └── method / dataset / experiment
  │
  ├── supports / contradicts / refines
  │
  ├── theory / model / mechanism
  │
  ├── implementation / protocol / technology
  │
  ├── patent / publication / organization / person
  │
  └── reusable Book Matter
              ↓
      transclusion / query / graph / portal
</pre>

Not every page needs every object or relation. The architecture should allow sophistication to emerge where the knowledge requires it.

This is the difference between '''a complicated mandatory schema''' and '''a composable semantic substrate'''.

== Maturation workflow ==

For each major V1 primitive or design family:

{| class="wikitable"
! Stage !! Question !! Output
|-
| 1. Preserve || What exact source, variants, revisions, callers, memberships, and historical context exist? || Provenance-complete V1 evidence
|-
| 2. Understand || What problem was the design trying to solve? || Explicit original job and constraints
|-
| 3. Identify signal || Which ideas, behaviors, language, or structures remain valuable? || Surviving design signals
|-
| 4. Mature primitive || What is the smallest coherent V2 primitive or composition of primitives? || Candidate V2 model
|-
| 5. Enhance || What can current MediaWiki/SMW/Cargo/Page Forms/modules/graphs/agents/tooling now do that V1 could not coherently realize? || Enhanced implementation design
|-
| 6. Integrate || How does the primitive connect to ontology, epistemics, Book Matter, navigation, provenance, and lifecycle? || Integrated architecture
|-
| 7. Validate || Can structure, semantics, references, expected behavior, and migration fidelity be tested? || Validation gate
|}

== Initial work programme ==

The next V2 architecture work should proceed by design family rather than by indiscriminate page rewriting.

=== Ontology and semantic schema ===
Audit V1 entity types, topics, properties, relationship types, imported vocabularies, semantic patterns, and alignment proposals against current V2 use. Produce explicit '''preserve / mature / defer / historical''' dispositions.

=== Epistemics and confidence trails ===
Recover the full V1 epistemic imagination, identify the structures behind confidence trails, evidence paths, uncertainty, falsification, perspective, review, and provenance, then determine which require properties, templates, subobjects, queries, or simply editorial grammar.

=== Book Matter and transclusion ===
Map V1 Book Matter proposals and actual page patterns to a scalable composition model. Preserve deep coherent parent pages while identifying genuinely reusable semantic units.

=== Templates, modules, and interfaces ===
Contrast documented templates/modules with actual transclusion and caller evidence. Mature repeated behavior; do not turn the WantedTemplates list into a backlog by default.

=== Portals, categories, indices, and graphs ===
Treat these as multiple views over shared knowledge rather than competing taxonomies. Develop each view around actual retrieval and orientation jobs.

=== Research and laboratory objects ===
Investigate how publications, patents, datasets, experiments, methods, claims, implementations, organizations, people, and research artifacts should participate in the knowledge graph without overfitting the base ontology prematurely.

== Architectural invariant ==

<blockquote>'''V1 imagination is source material, not technical debt. V2 coherence is a substrate, not a ceiling.'''</blockquote>

The purpose of V2 is to let the strongest V1 ideas become more operational, composable, inspectable, and extensible while retaining the intellectual character that made BITwiki worth building.

